<title>HUNGARY: Hungary's purchasing index (PMI) 57.8 pct in Oct.</title>
<headline>Hungary's purchasing index (PMI) 57.8 pct in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's Purchasing Manager Index (PMI) was 57.8 percent in October, down from 60.4 percent in September, but up from 52.7 percent in October 1995, the publisher of the index, the Hungarian Association of Logistics, Purchasing and Inventory Management said on Monday.  </p>
<p>PURCHASING MANAGER INDEX (PERCENT)</p>
<p>    1996 October		  57.8</p>
<p>	   September		60.4</p>
<p>	   August		   52.7</p>
<p>	   July		     48.5</p>
<p>	   June		     50.6</p>
<p>	   May			53.8</p>
<p>	   April		    51.4</p>
<p>	   March		    51.4</p>
<p>	   February		 55.6</p>
<p>	   January		  47.1</p>
<p>    1995 December		 35.9</p>
<p>	   November		 51.2</p>
<p>	   October		  52.7</p>
<p>NOTES: The PMI is calculated using the same methodology as the United States' National Association of Purchasing Management Index. A figure above 50 indicates increasing, a number below 50 declining economic activity.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
